---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout sideBarActiveItemID="home" title="Agueda Schwartz">
  <div class="mt-8 md:mt-16">
    <!-- Hero -->
    <section class="mb-12 md:mb-20">
      <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl md:text-7xl font-bold leading-[1.05] tracking-tight mb-6">Agueda Schwartz</h1>

      <div class="text-lg md:text-xl font-medium mb-4 -mt-2">Product Operations · Evaluation · AI-Native Delivery</div>

      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-3 gap-y-2 mb-8 text-base md:text-lg opacity-80">
        <span>📍 Queens, NY</span>
        <span class="opacity-40 hidden md:inline">·</span>
        <span>English &amp; Spanish</span>
        <span class="opacity-40 hidden md:inline">·</span>
        <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/amijach/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="LinkedIn" class="inline-flex items-center hover:opacity-100 transition-opacity">
          <svg class="w-5 h-5" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M20.447 20.452h-3.554v-5.569c0-1.328-.027-3.037-1.852-3.037-1.853 0-2.136 1.445-2.136 2.939v5.667H9.351V9h3.414v1.561h.046c.477-.9 1.637-1.85 3.37-1.85 3.601 0 4.267 2.37 4.267 5.455v6.286zM5.337 7.433a2.062 2.062 0 01-2.063-2.065 2.063 2.063 0 112.063 2.065zm1.782 13.019H3.555V9h3.564v11.452zM22.225 0H1.771C.792 0 0 .774 0 1.729v20.542C0 23.227.792 24 1.771 24h20.451C23.2 24 24 23.227 24 22.271V1.729C24 .774 23.2 0 22.222 0h.003z"/>
          </svg>
        </a>
        <a href="https://github.com/amijach1103" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="GitHub" class="inline-flex items-center hover:opacity-100 transition-opacity">
          <svg class="w-5 h-5" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M12 .297c-6.63 0-12 5.373-12 12 0 5.303 3.438 9.8 8.205 11.385.6.113.82-.258.82-.577 0-.285-.01-1.04-.015-2.04-3.338.724-4.042-1.61-4.042-1.61C4.422 18.07 3.633 17.7 3.633 17.7c-1.087-.744.084-.729.084-.729 1.205.084 1.838 1.236 1.838 1.236 1.07 1.835 2.809 1.305 3.495.998.108-.776.417-1.305.76-1.605-2.665-.3-5.466-1.332-5.466-5.93 0-1.31.465-2.38 1.235-3.22-.135-.303-.54-1.523.105-3.176 0 0 1.005-.322 3.3 1.23.96-.267 1.98-.399 3-.405 1.02.006 2.04.138 3 .405 2.28-1.552 3.285-1.23 3.285-1.23.645 1.653.24 2.873.12 3.176.765.84 1.23 1.91 1.23 3.22 0 4.61-2.805 5.625-5.475 5.92.42.36.81 1.096.81 2.22 0 1.606-.015 2.896-.015 3.286 0 .315.21.69.825.57C20.565 22.092 24 17.592 24 12.297c0-6.627-5.373-12-12-12"/>
          </svg>
        </a>
      </div>

      <p class="text-lg md:text-xl leading-relaxed max-w-3xl">
        I've spent my career on one question: does this actually work? I've asked it as program evaluation across twenty campuses in Peru, and lately about an AI product and the founders using it, and the answer has to be something a product team can act on and a leader can stand behind. That is evaluation, and it is the part I am actually known for: deciding what would count as working before anything is built, then measuring against it rather than against how much people used it. That work is harder now and it matters more: teams can ship faster than they can learn, and it's easy to let the model stand in for the person it was built for. Sixteen years of it, across K-12, professional services, and higher ed on two continents. I do this work because education should not be a privilege of the few, and neither should the technology that makes it better.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Three cards -->
    <section>
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 md:gap-6">
        <a href="/projects" class="block p-6 md:p-7 bg-base-200 rounded-lg hover:bg-base-300 transition-colors group">
          <div class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.15em] opacity-60 mb-2 font-semibold">Projects</div>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold mb-3 leading-snug">Deciding what was worth building</h2>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed mb-4">Four projects, from a 20-campus school network to a 0-to-1 AI product. What got kept, what got cut, and what the evidence was.</p>
          <div class="text-xs font-medium opacity-70 group-hover:opacity-100 transition-opacity">See projects →</div>
        </a>

        <a href="/practice" class="block p-6 md:p-7 bg-base-200 rounded-lg hover:bg-base-300 transition-colors group">
          <div class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.15em] opacity-60 mb-2 font-semibold">Practice</div>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold mb-3 leading-snug">How I work with AI</h2>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed mb-4">The system I built to run four tracks at once, and where I draw the line between what it owns and what I do.</p>
          <div class="text-xs font-medium opacity-70 group-hover:opacity-100 transition-opacity">See practice →</div>
        </a>

        <a href="/notes/" class="block p-6 md:p-7 bg-base-200 rounded-lg hover:bg-base-300 transition-colors group">
          <div class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.15em] opacity-60 mb-2 font-semibold">Notes</div>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold mb-3 leading-snug">What I'm learning as I work</h2>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed mb-4">Methods, experiments, failures, and signals. Less polished than Practice or Projects on purpose.</p>
          <div class="text-xs font-medium opacity-70 group-hover:opacity-100 transition-opacity">Read notes →</div>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style is:global>
  a:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid hsl(var(--bc));
    outline-offset: 2px;
    border-radius: 2px;
  }

  body {
    cursor: url('data:image/svg+xml;utf8,<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="32" height="32"><text x="2" y="26" font-size="24">%F0%9F%91%BE</text></svg>') 4 4, auto;
  }

  a, button, [role="button"], summary {
    cursor: url('data:image/svg+xml;utf8,<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="32" height="32"><text x="2" y="26" font-size="24">%F0%9F%91%BE</text></svg>') 4 4, pointer;
  }
</style>
